Dear Mayor Kaysen,
Cheyenne Frontier Days and its parade routes, produce a large gathering of visitors to Wyoming overa
10 day period.This event is monitored by the Department of Energy(DOE), Environmental Protection
Agency(EPA), Department of Defense(DOD), and state assets to assist in overall protection and
prevention should an event occur.This office assists with security elements under critical infrastructure
protection asit pertains to special events.The City of Cheyenne has requested the Wyoming Office of
Homeland Security's support for additional security camerasto coverhigh use areas of thecity,
especially during Cheyenne Frontier Days and the Union Pacificrail yards.These cameras will be placed
on the clocktower on the parking structure at thecornerof Carey Avenue and16th Street/Lincolnway
and on the new building in the Depot Plaza.
Please consider this letter as our offerto assist with the funding for these security cameras using our
State Homeland Security Grant, under infrastructure systems.The cost estimate provided to this office
for these projects is $15,000.00-$20,000.00 and periodic maintenance willbe provided by the City of
Cheyenne.
When theprojects are complete, please send us a bill with the total cost and the accompanying backup
documentation and we will reimburse the city for its cost.
Please feel free to calluswith any questions orconcerns.
Sincerely,
Guy Cameron, Director
Wy on king Office of Homeland Security
0L2012-0130
